# Ownership drives review routing. Two rules carry real weight.
#
# contracts/ requires review from both client and server owners, because a protocol change
# that only one side has read is how the two implementations drift, and on this system
# drift appears as silent data divergence rather than as a build failure.
#
# Anything touching the sync engine or the security model needs a second reader for the
# same reason: the failure modes are invisible until they are expensive.

*                                   @talif

/contracts/                         @talif
/ios/Packages/ApertureCore/Sources/ApertureSync/   @talif
/ios/Packages/AperturePlatform/Sources/ApertureSecurity/   @talif
/backend/internal/sync/             @talif
/backend/internal/tenancy/          @talif
/infra/                             @talif
/.github/workflows/                 @talif
